To register only the **minimal set of tools** required for `pine_set_source`, `pine_add_to_chart`, `strategy_tester_read_summary`, `data_get_trades`, and `data_get_equity`, we must identify dependencies and isolate core logic.

### Minimal Registration Hunk

```js
import { McpServer } from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/mcp.js";
import { StdioServerTransport } from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/stdio.js";
import { registerPineTools } from "./tools/pine.js";
import { registerDataTools } from "./tools/data.js";
import { registerLabTools } from "./tools/lab.js";

const server = new McpServer(
  {
    name: "tradingview",
    version: "2.0.0",
    description:
      "AI-assisted TradingView chart analysis and Pine Script development via Chrome DevTools Protocol",
  },
  {
    instructions: `Minimal MCP server for Pine + data tools.`,
  },
);

// Register only necessary tool groups
registerPineTools(server);
registerDataTools(server);
registerLabTools(server);

await server.connect(new StdioServerTransport());
```

### Required Dependencies

1. **`tools/pine.js`** – Contains `pine_set_source`, `pine_add_to_chart`.
2. **`tools/data.js`** – Contains `data_get_trades`, `data_get_equity`.
3. **`tools/lab.js`** – Contains `strategy_tester_read_summary`.

> No additional tools or dependencies are needed beyond these core modules.

This setup ensures only the listed tools are registered, with no live chart interaction or extra functionality.
